            "subject": "LU-20867 gss: re-resolve lsvcgssd ioctl device on failure"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 03:11:28.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-10-30 03:11:40.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: import zpool for writeconf_facet on ZFS",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: import zpool for writeconf_facet on ZFS\n\nwriteconf_facet stops the facet with -f, which exports the ZFS\npool, then runs tunefs.lustre --writeconf on a pool that is not\nimported. tunefs.lustre exits 19, and writeconf_or_reformat falls\nback to \"tunefs.lustre failed, reformatting instead\" on every\ncall, which costs a reformat and gen_config each time.\n\nImport the pool before tunefs.lustre and export it afterwards, as\nthe start path expects.\n\nconf-sanity on ZFS in a test VM, 257 tests, before and after:\n13 tests (21c 29 35a 46a 50c 50d 50f 50g 51 57a 57b 59 64) logged\nthe reformat fallback before and none do after. Their total run\ntime went from 900s to 607s (about 22s per fallback avoided). All\n257 tests have the same result before and after (tests 36, 117\nand 158 fail both ways).\n\nAt about 13 fallbacks per run and 2400 ZFS conf-sanity runs per\n30 days, the VM figure is about 195 hours saved per 30 days; CI\nreformats are slower than the VM's, so the CI saving is larger.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity fstype=zfs\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I3967a42f4bfbea067eed49a44ac2255a36ab7709\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
